WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.930
<b>Tsubame West High School</b>

00:00.830 --> 00:04.130
<i>Tsubame West High School's 
school festival is a huge affair.</i>

00:04.130 --> 00:06.810
<i>The committee spends 
all year planning for it.</i>

00:06.810 --> 00:09.980
<i>Many clubs put on exhibits.</i>

00:09.980 --> 00:12.530
<i>All first- and second-year classes 
run some kind of attraction.</i>

00:12.530 --> 00:15.800
<i>Third-year volunteers run stalls.</i>

00:15.800 --> 00:21.170
<i>The student council meets with 
the budget and equipment teams</i>

00:18.410 --> 00:21.620
<b>Tsubame West High School Festival</b>

00:21.170 --> 00:25.750
<i>and helps out wherever we're needed, 
meaning we're very busy.</i>

00:26.130 --> 00:30.630
<i>Which is why I haven't been present 
for a lot of my class's play rehearsals.</i>

00:31.240 --> 00:33.260
<i>By the way, the play we're performing...</i>

00:42.340 --> 00:45.720
<i>So dazzling</i>

00:45.720 --> 00:49.160
<i>I find myself looking away</i>

00:49.880 --> 00:52.780
<i>Unable to find the right words</i>

00:52.780 --> 00:55.570
<i>Even a single word to say</i>

01:09.920 --> 01:12.640
<i>In such a narrow world</i>

01:12.640 --> 01:16.430
<i>Your vibrant laughter</i>

01:16.430 --> 01:19.390
<i>Resonates so beautifully</i>

01:19.390 --> 01:22.200
<i>And that's what saved me</i>

01:22.640 --> 01:26.300
<i>If we relive this moment</i>

01:26.300 --> 01:29.520
<i>In an unimaginable future</i>

01:29.520 --> 01:32.490
<i>Even if we're lost, it's okay</i>

01:32.490 --> 01:36.330
<i>We will be in it together</i>

01:37.020 --> 01:40.320
<i>So dazzling</i>

01:40.320 --> 01:44.120
<i>I find myself looking away</i>

01:44.490 --> 01:47.410
<i>Unable to find the right words</i>

01:47.410 --> 01:50.240
<i>Even a single word to say</i>

01:50.240 --> 01:53.570
<i>I was entranced</i>

01:53.570 --> 01:57.680
<i>By your lively figure</i>

01:57.680 --> 02:00.830
<i>If the true nature of this blue warmth</i>

02:00.830 --> 02:03.610
<i>Is love, then…</i>

02:04.340 --> 02:07.470
<i>If the true nature of this blue warmth</i>

02:07.470 --> 02:10.250
<i>Is love, then...</i>

02:11.980 --> 02:23.740
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

02:11.980 --> 02:23.740
<b>"The Family Singers"
performed by Tsubame West High School Class 1-3

Dates: Nov 3 (Sat) & Nov 4 (Sun)

Morning Showing:		Afternoon Showing:
Venue: Classroom Wing 3F Class 1-3</b>

02:12.680 --> 02:15.520
<i>The play we're performing 
is "The Family Singers,"</i>

02:15.520 --> 02:19.790
<i>the story of a family 
published several decades ago.</i>

02:19.790 --> 02:22.350
<i>After release, it was translated 
all over the world.</i>

02:22.350 --> 02:25.090
<i>It's a timeless musical, 
beloved to this day.</i>

02:25.090 --> 02:29.000
<i>We're going to put on an original 
play based on the story.</i>

02:29.470 --> 02:31.230
<i>When we were deciding on our attraction,</i>

02:31.230 --> 02:34.500
<i>Asano-san, our class's 
school festival rep said...</i>

02:34.500 --> 02:38.540
The thing is, I came here to see the school 
festival when I was in middle school.

02:38.540 --> 02:40.870
I knew I wanted to enroll here right away.

02:40.870 --> 02:44.890
Everything was so high-quality, and all 
the students were having so much fun.

02:45.270 --> 02:49.190
And it's always been my dream 
to do a musical as a class!

02:50.010 --> 02:51.590
What do you guys think?

02:51.590 --> 02:54.830
I'll take on all the troublesome work!

02:59.800 --> 03:01.990
When you put it like that, how can we say no?

03:01.990 --> 03:03.990
Time's a-wasting! Let's get to it!

03:04.470 --> 03:06.450
I wanted to do a musical, too!

03:06.450 --> 03:08.700
Heck yeah! This is gonna rule!

03:08.700 --> 03:12.260
<i>It's going to be tough, 
but I'm sure it'll be a great success.</i>

03:12.260 --> 03:14.130
<i>That's the feeling I get.</i>

03:16.380 --> 03:20.130
Uh, that's some crazy motivation 
for a school event.

03:20.130 --> 03:22.260
Right? It's crazy.

03:22.260 --> 03:23.690
Even I was surprised.

03:23.690 --> 03:25.500
I guess every school's different.

03:25.500 --> 03:29.130
Last year, a couple got handsy 
in the dark at our school,

03:29.130 --> 03:31.520
so haunted houses are banned this year.

03:32.040 --> 03:33.350
By the way, what're you doing?

03:33.350 --> 03:34.860
Uh...

03:34.860 --> 03:36.350
No way, you're in the cast?!

03:36.350 --> 03:38.860
It kind of just happened...

03:39.290 --> 03:41.900
What, you couldn't refuse?

03:41.900 --> 03:45.210
Nah, I could've said no, but...

03:45.210 --> 03:48.990
<i>What? I'm not acting. 
I'll work on the set and stuff.</i>

03:49.980 --> 03:51.730
Join us, Shima!

03:51.730 --> 03:54.110
Nah, I don't sing...

03:53.500 --> 03:58.840
<b></b>Wants to stand out

03:54.110 --> 03:57.190
Oh, come on! You're okay at karaoke!

03:57.190 --> 03:58.840
Let's make some memories, dude!

03:58.840 --> 04:00.500
Me! Me! I'll do it!

04:00.500 --> 04:01.990
Nice, Suda-chan!

04:01.990 --> 04:04.400
No shame if we're all in it!

04:05.230 --> 04:06.830
<i>W-Wait...</i>

04:06.830 --> 04:11.070
<i>I'm supposed to be the guy 
who says yes to everything?</i>

04:11.460 --> 04:15.790
<i>Wouldn't they find it weird if I refused 
to perform for a little school festival?</i>

04:17.930 --> 04:19.020
Y...

04:19.020 --> 04:21.410
Yeah, you're right. I'll do it.

04:21.410 --> 04:23.490
Now we're talking!

04:23.490 --> 04:24.930
Paranoid.

04:24.930 --> 04:25.860
Yeah.

04:25.860 --> 04:29.890
Looking back, I could've 
gotten out of it, easy.

04:29.890 --> 04:33.240
Sousuke, do you have any 
friends at your school?

04:33.240 --> 04:35.040
Huh? Of course I do.

04:35.040 --> 04:39.920
But if you're more concerned about 
breaking character than your own feelings,

04:39.920 --> 04:42.670
you're gonna snap at some point.

04:42.670 --> 04:44.510
It'll take a toll on you,

04:44.510 --> 04:47.050
and they'll notice that 
you're not being honest.

04:47.050 --> 04:48.980
And that you're distancing yourself.

04:50.010 --> 04:53.240
We'll do rehearsals during 
lunch and after school.

04:53.240 --> 04:54.430
Hey.

04:53.240 --> 04:57.990
If you guys have any suggestions 
regarding your characters, let us know.

04:54.430 --> 04:56.360
You sure you want to do this?

04:56.360 --> 04:58.960
Well, you know, I'll live.

04:59.840 --> 05:02.190
As long as it doesn't bother you.

05:02.900 --> 05:04.290
You may have a point.

05:04.290 --> 05:05.460
Knew it.

05:05.460 --> 05:09.700
But I'm more comfortable 
keeping a little distance.

05:09.700 --> 05:13.700
I don't want them prying 
into my child actor days.

05:13.700 --> 05:16.890
and I don't wanna make 
Ririka's life any harder.

05:16.890 --> 05:21.460
If that means I'm "secretive" 
and can't make any real friends,

05:21.810 --> 05:23.470
then it is what it is.

05:24.210 --> 05:27.050
That's not what I'm talking about.

05:27.050 --> 05:29.480
But sorry, let's drop it. Want a cherry?

05:29.480 --> 05:30.890
Huh? No thanks.

05:31.400 --> 05:32.890
It's all soggy and gross.

05:34.060 --> 05:37.110
Oh, don't tell Ririka 
about the school festival.

05:37.110 --> 05:38.190
Of course.

05:38.190 --> 05:40.860
Sousuke, in a musical?!

05:40.860 --> 05:43.030
That'll be a riot! When is it?

05:43.770 --> 05:46.330
Well, I'll just take it easy.

05:47.330 --> 05:48.610
You always had so much fun.

05:49.870 --> 05:53.290
More than any of us. Back then, I mean.

05:54.030 --> 05:55.160
Like...

05:55.160 --> 05:58.420
I'm sure it sucked when the work dried up.

05:58.920 --> 06:03.070
But you were so good 
that it never should have.

06:03.070 --> 06:05.340
So, like...

06:05.340 --> 06:07.130
Don't worry too much and just enjoy it.

06:10.020 --> 06:12.900
You're such a bro, Chris-kun.

06:12.900 --> 06:14.220
Aren't I?

06:14.780 --> 06:16.170
Oops. I farted.

06:16.170 --> 06:17.770
Ew...

06:22.980 --> 06:26.110
<b>Set and Props</b>

06:23.380 --> 06:24.790
Cut it straight down.

06:24.790 --> 06:26.110
Got it.

06:26.110 --> 06:28.350
Sorry, could you get the white?

06:26.110 --> 06:29.990
<b>Painting</b>

06:28.350 --> 06:29.990
Okay, just a sec.

06:29.990 --> 06:32.990
<b>Costumes</b>

06:32.990 --> 06:35.490
We'll change the lights, like, bang!

06:32.990 --> 06:37.660
<b>Lighting and Sound</b>

06:35.490 --> 06:37.280
So I up the volume?

06:37.660 --> 06:40.920
<b>Budget</b>

06:40.920 --> 06:42.940
Can we hand all of these out?

06:40.920 --> 06:45.170
<b>Advertising</b>

06:42.940 --> 06:45.170
We should put some signs up, too.

06:45.860 --> 06:51.400
<i>In a small European country, 
in the days leading up to war...</i>

06:51.400 --> 06:54.590
<i>As a shadow of unrest blankets the world,</i>

06:54.590 --> 06:58.480
<i>the people here spend 
their final days of peace.</i>

06:59.380 --> 07:03.310
Please let me stay here! 
This is my home, my life!

07:00.060 --> 07:03.310
<b>Lyra
Asano Ryouko</b>

07:03.310 --> 07:06.580
Look yourself in the mirror, Lyra.

07:03.440 --> 07:06.940
<b>The Mother Abbess
Egashira Mika</b>

07:06.940 --> 07:11.230
<i>Lyra, a nun in training, 
is a free spirit who loves singing.</i>

07:11.230 --> 07:14.450
<i>For being a rule-breaker at the convent,</i>

07:14.450 --> 07:17.200
<i>she is sent to the Captain's 
manor as a tutor.</i>

07:17.200 --> 07:22.960
<b>Eldest Son
Enomoto Tomoki</b>

07:17.200 --> 07:22.960
<b>Eldest Daughter
Nagata Youka</b>

07:17.200 --> 07:22.960
<b>Second Son
Suda Shunya</b>

07:17.200 --> 07:22.960
<b>Second Daughter
Motobayashi Yukina</b>

07:17.200 --> 07:22.960
<b>Third Daughter
Tamaki Hikari</b>

07:17.200 --> 07:22.960
<b>Fourth Daughter
Mine Asuka</b>

07:17.200 --> 07:22.960
<b>Fifth Daughter
Koshiba Nene</b>

07:17.610 --> 07:22.270
<i>The Captain had many children, 
but ever since his wife's passing,</i>

07:22.270 --> 07:25.280
<i>he struggled to face his family.</i>

07:25.710 --> 07:29.470
<b>Captain
Hashimoto Takumi</b>

07:25.710 --> 07:29.470
I have work to do. Take care of the children.

07:29.970 --> 07:31.720
<b>The Captain's Fiancée
Jougasaki Mayuri</b>

07:29.970 --> 07:31.720
<b>Butler
Yamada Kento</b>

07:30.370 --> 07:35.960
<i>Can Lyra bring song and laughter 
back to this family?!</i>

07:37.170 --> 07:38.410
Johan!

07:37.970 --> 07:39.980
<b>Captain's Niece, Emilia
Kinomoto Koharu</b>

07:38.410 --> 07:39.980
<i>The Captain's niece, Emilia...</i>

07:40.400 --> 07:41.730
<i>And Johan, the gardener.</i>

07:41.730 --> 07:44.230
<i>What will become of their forbidden love?!</i>

07:44.980 --> 07:47.110
<b>Gardener Johan
Shima Sousuke</b>

07:45.270 --> 07:47.110
Lady Emilia!

07:48.560 --> 07:54.560
<i>I have found you, my little rose.</i>

07:54.560 --> 08:00.430
<i>You face the raging storms, 
how brave you are.</i>

08:00.430 --> 08:03.830
<i>I'll take care of you.</i>

08:03.830 --> 08:11.930
<i>Come take my hand, my little rose.</i>

08:11.010 --> 08:14.760
<b>Also Directing</b>

08:14.760 --> 08:18.040
Yes! That was perfect, you two!

08:18.040 --> 08:20.140
We've got the award in the bag already!

08:20.140 --> 08:22.280
That got my heart racing!

08:22.280 --> 08:24.190
Sorry my hand hit you.

08:24.190 --> 08:25.480
It's all good.

08:25.480 --> 08:26.520
<i>Ugh.</i>

08:27.630 --> 08:29.980
<i>Must be nice, playing the love interest.</i>

08:30.490 --> 08:32.640
<i>But those two are perfect for their roles.</i>

08:32.640 --> 08:35.360
<i>Kinomoto-san is in the dance club, 
and she can sing.</i>

08:35.820 --> 08:38.140
<i>Above all, Kinomoto-san has a boyfriend,</i>

08:38.140 --> 08:40.080
<i>and everyone knows 
they're crazy for each other.</i>

08:40.080 --> 08:42.300
<i>That's why there was no backlash 
from the other girls.</i>

08:42.300 --> 08:44.190
Take care of Koharu for me!

08:42.370 --> 08:46.750
<b>Peace Treaty</b>

08:44.190 --> 08:46.750
<i>Well, nobody actually said that, 
but that has to be it!</i>

08:47.290 --> 08:49.670
Oh, wow. You're rehearsing already.

08:49.670 --> 08:50.750
Welcome back.

08:50.750 --> 08:54.150
Nishino-kun, can you pass 
these out to everyone?

08:54.150 --> 08:55.150
Sure.

08:55.150 --> 08:58.120
<i>Does Mitsumi really get it?</i>

08:56.780 --> 08:59.150
But can it wait until after rehearsal?

08:58.120 --> 08:59.740
<i>I get she's busy and all,</i>

08:59.150 --> 09:01.480
Yeah, no problem.

08:59.740 --> 09:02.390
<i>but school festival magic is very real.</i>

09:04.420 --> 09:05.360
<i>Wait, no!</i>

09:05.360 --> 09:07.650
<i>That's none of my concern.</i>

09:07.650 --> 09:09.810
Yikes, I got paint on me.

09:09.810 --> 09:11.610
I'll go get some more boxes.

09:12.640 --> 09:14.530
<i>That looks like fun.</i>

09:15.150 --> 09:18.190
<i>Third-year classes don't host attractions,</i>

09:18.190 --> 09:20.850
<i>so we only have this and next year.</i>

09:20.850 --> 09:22.550
<i>Behind-the-scenes work is fun,</i>

09:22.550 --> 09:25.290
<i>but I wish I could've 
done something here, too.</i>

09:25.290 --> 09:28.220
Hmm, we can't cut this part...

09:28.220 --> 09:29.580
Asano-san.

09:29.580 --> 09:31.850
Let me know if you need help with anything.

09:31.850 --> 09:33.160
Really? You're sure?!

09:33.160 --> 09:35.970
In that case, we keep running over time.

09:35.970 --> 09:39.770
We're gonna take one last look at the 
screenplay and talk about it tomorrow.

09:39.770 --> 09:41.760
Could you weigh in, Iwakura-san?

09:42.380 --> 09:44.770
This is a video of yesterday's run-through,

09:44.770 --> 09:46.890
and this is the script.

09:46.890 --> 09:48.770
<i>Wow, this is a big job.</i>

09:48.770 --> 09:51.580
Oh, but I know you're busy.

09:51.580 --> 09:53.030
It's okay if you can't.

09:53.030 --> 09:54.630
No worries!

09:54.630 --> 09:57.820
I think I can make the meeting 
if it's before school or during lunch.

09:57.820 --> 10:01.040
Ooh, I knew I could count on you! Thank you!

10:01.040 --> 10:02.020
Not at all.

10:02.020 --> 10:04.080
I wanted to help out, too.

10:05.900 --> 10:09.700
<i>But I took the pamphlets home and 
worked on them last night as well.</i>

10:09.700 --> 10:11.500
<i>I'm a little sleepy.</i>

10:12.280 --> 10:13.250
Watch out!

10:13.560 --> 10:14.630
You okay?

10:16.200 --> 10:19.870
Hey, careful! We're using nails here.

10:19.870 --> 10:21.220
S-S-S-S-Sorry!

10:21.220 --> 10:24.440
Right. You're somehow making do 
with the wood we have.

10:24.440 --> 10:26.050
Breaking it would be a disaster.

10:26.050 --> 10:28.160
You must be tired, Mitsumi-chan.

10:28.160 --> 10:29.690
Maybe you should take a break?

10:30.060 --> 10:32.020
I'm just fine! Thanks!

10:32.020 --> 10:34.520
I mean, I think you're 
taking on too much work.

10:34.520 --> 10:36.400
Maybe you could delegate some?

10:36.400 --> 10:38.900
I'm having fun doing it, so it's fine.

10:38.900 --> 10:40.900
I like being depended on.

10:40.900 --> 10:45.320
And it's such a big event. 
I want to experience it all.

10:45.690 --> 10:47.040
I see.

10:47.040 --> 10:49.040
Well, good luck with rehearsal!

10:49.040 --> 10:49.950
Thanks.

10:53.070 --> 10:54.450
<i>And cut!</i>

10:54.450 --> 10:57.920
That'll do. It was great.

10:57.920 --> 11:00.080
Let's take a quick breather.

11:02.180 --> 11:03.490
Mom!

11:03.490 --> 11:04.970
Were you watching?

11:04.970 --> 11:06.930
I sure was, Sousuke.

11:06.930 --> 11:10.690
You were amazing. 
You really gave it your all.

11:11.580 --> 11:14.490
<i>Why did I remember that?</i>

11:15.190 --> 11:19.190
<b>Tsubame West High School Festival
Popularity Vote Ballot</b>

11:16.020 --> 11:19.190
Whoa, what now? Voting ballots?

11:19.190 --> 11:22.430
Yep. They needed extras on the double.

11:22.430 --> 11:24.640
Just don't overwork yourself, okay?

11:24.640 --> 11:25.640
Okay.

11:26.010 --> 11:27.220
Good night!

11:27.220 --> 11:28.390
Yeah.

11:30.430 --> 11:33.460
<i>Oh, right. I need to watch 
the rehearsal video, too.</i>

11:47.150 --> 11:48.470
Sorry! Good morning!

11:48.470 --> 11:50.580
Good morning, Iwakura-san.

11:50.580 --> 11:51.740
Meeting!

11:51.740 --> 11:53.600
We're wrapping up. The bell's about to ring.

11:54.170 --> 11:56.450
Well? Any good ideas?

11:56.450 --> 11:58.270
Actually, uh...

11:58.270 --> 11:59.430
I'm really sorry!

11:59.430 --> 12:02.360
I fell asleep yesterday! 
I didn't get to watch very much...

12:02.360 --> 12:04.110
Oh, gotcha.

12:04.110 --> 12:05.660
It happens.

12:05.660 --> 12:09.160
<i>I screwed up!</i>

12:09.160 --> 12:10.650
What's for lunch?

12:10.650 --> 12:12.030
I could eat a horse!

12:12.030 --> 12:14.030
<i>I could still watch it now...</i>

12:14.030 --> 12:16.530
Mitsumi, let's have lunch.

12:16.530 --> 12:17.790
Yeah...

12:17.790 --> 12:19.780
Oh, this might work!

12:19.780 --> 12:20.510
Asano-san!

12:20.510 --> 12:22.170
I think she's in the courtyard.

12:22.170 --> 12:23.610
I'll be back real quick!

12:23.610 --> 12:24.550
Huh? What about lunch?

12:24.550 --> 12:26.770
Sorry! Start without me!

12:35.370 --> 12:38.350
If she didn't watch it, what was 
the point of rushing to school?

12:38.350 --> 12:40.040
Iwakura-san, huh?

12:45.490 --> 12:47.820
Iwakura-san's always running.

12:52.220 --> 12:53.170
Shima?

12:53.990 --> 12:56.290
<i>Now I know why I remembered that.</i>

12:57.590 --> 13:00.050
<i>She's always on the brink 
of tripping and getting hurt.</i>

13:00.050 --> 13:03.370
If she couldn't do it, 
she shouldn't have said yes at all.

13:03.370 --> 13:05.230
Well, you know.

13:05.230 --> 13:07.860
She's kinda, like, running around in circles.

13:09.550 --> 13:11.860
<i>Like a small child.</i>

13:12.970 --> 13:16.980
<u>Scene 10: Scrambling and Dripping</u>

13:16.980 --> 13:19.480
<b>Kanade: "Fireflies can only be seen at night, right?"</b>

13:20.010 --> 13:22.260
You didn't need to call 
my workplace about it!

13:22.260 --> 13:24.990
Then you shouldn't have lied 
about your business trip!

13:24.990 --> 13:27.100
How am I in the wrong here?

13:27.100 --> 13:27.860
Forget it.

13:32.570 --> 13:33.780
Mom?

13:35.230 --> 13:36.620
What's wrong?

13:37.410 --> 13:40.810
It's fine. We just had a little fight.

13:40.810 --> 13:41.630
Really?

13:42.610 --> 13:43.820
Really.

13:45.540 --> 13:50.790
M-Mom, I memorized my
next line and the one after!

13:51.220 --> 13:53.450
That's amazing, Sousuke.

13:53.450 --> 13:55.070
Weren't there some long ones, too?

13:55.070 --> 13:57.130
I can say them. You wanna hear?

13:58.860 --> 14:01.290
Fireflies can only be seen at night, right?

14:01.290 --> 14:05.610
So let's all sneak out at night 
and go to the river.

14:05.610 --> 14:09.170
We'll go by ourselves, 
without telling the grown-ups.

14:09.170 --> 14:11.290
I'll think of the plan.

14:11.290 --> 14:14.240
The nurses always go on patrol 
at the same time.

14:14.240 --> 14:15.820
Once every hour.

14:16.970 --> 14:20.630
We'll sneak past the nurse station 
while they're gone, and...

14:22.130 --> 14:25.790
<i>Johan the gardener falls into 
a forbidden love with Emilia.</i>

14:25.790 --> 14:30.070
<i>But, enticed by a man he respects, 
he serves the fascists.</i>

14:30.070 --> 14:32.980
<i>And his earnest nature 
doesn't allow him to back out.</i>

14:33.640 --> 14:37.780
<i>He's desperate to believe his cause is just, 
but he lacks conviction and faith.</i>

14:38.640 --> 14:41.020
<i>In the end, crushed by his immense guilt,</i>

14:41.020 --> 14:43.130
<i>he turns his back on the family 
and runs away.</i>

14:43.860 --> 14:47.060
<i>It's the perfect role for me, really.</i>

14:48.030 --> 14:50.480
Do you think we'll even make it?

14:50.480 --> 14:54.780
Right? We don't have much 
time left, thinking about it.

14:57.080 --> 14:58.390
What would you like?

14:59.160 --> 15:02.540
I worked part-time over summer break, 
and I am blessed with good fortune.

15:02.540 --> 15:04.380
Select the beverage of thy choosing.

15:04.380 --> 15:06.590
Huh? You're suddenly a lord?

15:06.590 --> 15:08.550
Uh... In that case...

15:08.550 --> 15:10.550
<b>Mandarin Jelly Juice</b>

15:08.920 --> 15:10.550
Mandarin jelly.

15:13.890 --> 15:16.760
Can you believe it's October?

15:16.760 --> 15:18.020
Yeah.

15:19.050 --> 15:22.270
<i>Didn't I pass by Shima-kun earlier?</i>

15:23.060 --> 15:30.110
<i>That means he overheard Asano-san 
talking and came back to check on me?</i>

15:30.110 --> 15:31.780
<i>He's so nice.</i>

15:33.150 --> 15:34.990
Sorry, I spaced out!

15:35.410 --> 15:38.090
Oh, right. I saw the video of the rehearsal.

15:38.090 --> 15:38.700
Ah...

15:38.700 --> 15:42.080
Your Johan was really great!

15:43.480 --> 15:46.970
Come on... Johan isn't great at all.

15:48.660 --> 15:51.670
Class 3 will be putting on a play!

15:52.470 --> 15:53.820
I'll do it.

15:53.820 --> 15:55.870
Now we're talking!

15:55.870 --> 15:59.020
With all due respect to Senpai, 
I don't wanna act anymore.

16:00.280 --> 16:04.660
I did give it my all back then, 
but not because I found it fun...

16:05.660 --> 16:08.130
But because it made my mom happy.

16:14.230 --> 16:16.200
Huh? Huh?!

16:16.910 --> 16:18.990
Shi... So...

16:19.450 --> 16:21.300
Huh? What?

16:21.300 --> 16:22.710
He's making her cry...

16:22.710 --> 16:24.170
He made a girl cry.

16:24.170 --> 16:25.330
What?!

16:28.030 --> 16:29.880
Feeling better?

16:29.880 --> 16:30.810
Yeah.

16:31.880 --> 16:35.290
Shima-kun, you didn't want to 
be in the play at all, did you?

16:35.290 --> 16:36.470
Uh...

16:37.170 --> 16:41.550
You told me about your past, 
so I should've known...

16:41.980 --> 16:45.390
Actually, I even thought something was wrong,

16:45.390 --> 16:48.360
but I told myself it was no big deal.

16:48.850 --> 16:50.200
I'm really sorry.

16:50.200 --> 16:54.110
Hey, no! It's all my fault 
for not being clear!

16:54.110 --> 16:58.250
No, like, that's not all.

16:58.250 --> 17:01.870
You heard what they were 
saying in the courtyard, right?

17:02.260 --> 17:06.720
I took on a job myself and failed to deliver.

17:06.720 --> 17:10.500
I had the desire, but I did 
the opposite of helping out.

17:10.500 --> 17:16.010
Meanwhile, you're worrying about me when 
you're dealing with problems of your own.

17:16.590 --> 17:22.020
Now I see... I wasn't thinking 
about anyone but myself.

17:22.020 --> 17:24.770
You don't need to let it get you that down...

17:29.870 --> 17:32.460
<i>I'm sure it's a big deal to her,</i>

17:33.650 --> 17:35.500
<i>but I can't believe she'd cry over this.</i>

17:36.060 --> 17:39.160
<i>The more people in your life, 
the more conflicts you'll have.</i>

17:39.160 --> 17:41.050
<i>This isn't even that bad.</i>

17:42.050 --> 17:46.740
<i>Are you really sure you want to be 
in Tokyo and in politics?</i>

17:47.630 --> 17:51.680
<i>Sure, my high school life 
is more fun with you around,</i>

17:52.120 --> 17:56.300
<i>but I feel like you'd be happier 
by the mountains and the sea.</i>

17:57.270 --> 17:58.800
<i>I want you to never get hurt</i>

17:59.910 --> 18:03.130
<i>and stay just the way you are.</i>

18:06.180 --> 18:10.990
Oh, but I really meant it when 
I said your Johan was great.

18:10.990 --> 18:14.190
The dance with Emilia was really cute.

18:14.190 --> 18:16.440
Oh, thanks.

18:16.440 --> 18:21.020
Can someone really report 
someone they love so much?

18:21.020 --> 18:23.650
That's the problem with Johan.

18:23.650 --> 18:26.450
That's why he goes over to the dark side.

18:27.870 --> 18:30.710
But no one dies in the end.

18:30.710 --> 18:32.110
He can still turn back.

18:33.090 --> 18:36.970
Emilia's supposed to be 
the same age as us, right?

18:36.970 --> 18:40.220
And Johan's only a year apart.

18:40.670 --> 18:45.840
I'd like to believe the story didn't want 
to show the paths they took in the end.

18:48.140 --> 18:49.890
Maybe.

18:51.070 --> 18:52.570
Want to give it a try?

18:52.570 --> 18:53.270
Huh?

18:57.090 --> 19:03.330
<i>I have found you, my little rose.</i>

19:03.330 --> 19:09.520
<i>You face the raging storms, 
how brave you are.</i>

19:09.520 --> 19:16.290
<i>Come take my hand, my little rose.</i>

19:16.290 --> 19:18.470
Okay, this is where Emilia stands up.

19:20.430 --> 19:21.380
Sing.

19:22.930 --> 19:28.960
<i>You plucked me, a little rose.</i>

19:28.960 --> 19:32.330
Something... hm-hm-hm...

19:33.160 --> 19:34.980
I don't know how it goes.

19:37.280 --> 19:39.820
Now, up the stairs and...

19:41.910 --> 19:45.620
<i>Your little rose.</i>

19:49.200 --> 19:51.530
That was embarrassing, but it was fun!

19:51.530 --> 19:53.210
You're really good, Mitsumi-chan.

19:55.680 --> 19:57.210
Thanks, Shima-kun.

19:57.210 --> 19:59.450
I'm all better now.

19:59.450 --> 20:00.670
Let's head back to class.

20:01.750 --> 20:04.100
You don't want to stop by the nurse's office?

20:04.100 --> 20:04.970
Why?

20:04.970 --> 20:07.870
Won't it be awkward? Like, with Asano-san.

20:07.870 --> 20:10.480
A little, but I have 
something to tell her, too.

20:12.680 --> 20:14.230
You know, Shima-kun...

20:14.690 --> 20:17.730
I'm the kind of person 
who falls flat on her face a lot.

20:18.190 --> 20:22.530
But that makes me a pro at dusting 
myself off and getting back up!

20:31.150 --> 20:32.150
Yeah.

20:33.580 --> 20:36.480
<i>That's just who Mitsumi-chan is.</i>

20:37.960 --> 20:41.400
Ugh... We're still going over an hour...

20:41.400 --> 20:42.630
Asano-san.

20:43.660 --> 20:47.210
Sorry, I couldn't figure out anything 
for the screenplay at a glance.

20:47.210 --> 20:48.580
Oh, that's okay.

20:48.580 --> 20:53.400
But if you use a set like this 
on stage, you could save time.

20:53.400 --> 20:54.310
Like what?

20:55.970 --> 20:58.560
Yeah! And it won't cost anything.

20:58.560 --> 21:00.110
Is this helpful?

21:00.110 --> 21:01.160
Totally!

21:01.610 --> 21:03.070
Shima-kun.

21:03.070 --> 21:04.700
We're reading the second half.

21:04.700 --> 21:06.200
Coming!

21:06.820 --> 21:09.200
<b>30 days until the school festival!</b>

21:09.200 --> 21:13.330
Happy birthday to you!

21:13.330 --> 21:15.340
Happy birthday, Shima!

21:15.340 --> 21:17.460
Whoa, thanks!

21:17.460 --> 21:21.150
<i>My little rose.</i>

21:21.630 --> 21:24.880
You're finally the same age 
as Emilia-tan. How cute.

21:23.340 --> 21:24.880
<b>Born in August</b>

21:24.880 --> 21:27.920
Oww! Dude, it wasn't that bad!

21:24.880 --> 21:29.890
<b>Cobra Twist</b>

21:27.920 --> 21:29.890
Well, I still felt like it.

21:29.890 --> 21:37.480
<b>28 days until the school festival!</b>

21:36.310 --> 21:45.860
<b>27 days until the school festival!</b>

21:44.860 --> 21:54.790
<b>22 days until the school festival!</b>

21:47.660 --> 21:51.920
<i>A gentle breeze, the setting sun</i>

21:51.920 --> 21:56.240
<i>Today was another good day</i>

21:54.200 --> 22:00.590
<b>18 days until the school festival!</b>

21:56.240 --> 22:00.580
<i>Forgetting all the plans I made</i>

21:59.790 --> 22:04.590
<b>7 days until the school festival!</b>

22:00.580 --> 22:04.590
<i>I'll walk to the next station over</i>

22:04.590 --> 22:09.260
<i>The more I trip and fall</i>

22:09.260 --> 22:13.270
<i>The better I get at picking myself back up</i>

22:13.270 --> 22:17.840
<i>Through honest dialogue and heart-to-hearts</i>

22:17.840 --> 22:22.240
<i>The warmth seeps into my soul</i>

22:22.240 --> 22:26.530
<i>Humming as I take the roundabout way</i>

22:26.530 --> 22:30.660
<i>My world is an unsolved mystery</i>

22:30.660 --> 22:35.170
<i>Top speed, toes and heels, strides</i>

22:35.170 --> 22:39.330
<i>Each one of us walks differently</i>

22:39.330 --> 22:43.850
<i>All the same, we wave goodbye to dusk</i>

22:43.850 --> 22:47.840
<i>As a new morning dawns</i>

22:47.840 --> 22:52.510
<i>Wanting to protect this everyday life</i>

22:52.510 --> 22:55.730
<i>With a hop, jump, and skip</i>

22:55.730 --> 22:58.980
<i>See you tomorrow</i>

23:10.660 --> 23:13.660
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

23:10.660 --> 23:13.660
<b>"The Family Singers"
performed by Tsubame West High School Class 1-3

Dates: Nov 3 (Sat) & Nov 4 (Sun)

Morning Showing:		Afternoon Showing:
Venue: Classroom Wing 3F Class 1-3</b>

23:15.660 --> 23:17.910
<b>1 day until the school festival!</b>

23:17.220 --> 23:19.380
If you'll excuse me, Uncle.

23:19.380 --> 23:20.420
Very well.

23:20.420 --> 23:24.790
I have an announcement. There is 
someone I would like to marry.

23:25.110 --> 23:26.740
You always had so much fun.

23:26.740 --> 23:28.050
More than any of us.

23:34.640 --> 23:39.980
<b>Tsubame West School Festival</b>
